{
  "_meta": {
    "notes": [
      "developer.indeed.com (the historical developer portal) 301-redirects to https://partners.indeed.com/, which then returns Cloudflare-mitigated 403 to non-browser user-agents. Effectively no public developer surface remains.",
      "www.indeed.com publishes a real, sophisticated /llms.txt (737 lines, lists ~23 named AI bots) but Indeed's Cloudflare WAF returns 403 to the agentsfirst.dev scorer's default user-agent on /llms.txt, /AGENTS.md, and most other paths. The artifact exists; the agent cannot fetch it. This is the report's core narrative.",
      "employers.indeed.com /robots.txt is 25 bytes: 'User-agent: *\\nDisallow: /' — the entire B2B surface declines crawling outright."
    ],
    "rubric_source": "https://github.com/capitalthought/agentsfirst/blob/main/tools/agentsfirst-mcp/src/score.ts",
    "rubric_version": "v0.1.2",
